## ArcGIS FeatureServer — Implementation Plan

### Overview

A new layer type `arcgis-feature` will be introduced in MapStore2. FeatureServer sub-layers will be discovered via the existing ArcGIS catalog, rendered as vector features in both OpenLayers and CesiumJS, and fully integrated with identify, style editor, legend, and map persistence.

All requests to ArcGIS will use `inSR=4326` / `outSR=4326` and `f=geojson`. Projection handling will be done entirely client-side via proj4 (registered by MapStore at startup), so **any custom projection** configured in `projectionDefs` will be supported without requiring ArcGIS to recognize the WKID.

---

### 1. Catalog — FeatureServer endpoint discovery

- `FeatureServer` will be added to the service type filter alongside `MapServer` / `ImageServer`.
- FeatureServer root metadata (`layers[]`) will be parsed into individual catalog records — one per sub-layer. Tables (no geometry) will be filtered out.
- Each record will carry: `id`, `name`, `geometryType`, `maxRecordCount`, `bbox`.
- `extentToBoundingBox` will register WKT-defined spatial references with proj4 before reprojecting to EPSG:4326, supporting services with custom spatial references .
- Layer of `type: 'arcgis-feature'` with `strategy: 'tile'` as default is produced

**`esriGeometryTypeToGeoJSON` mapping:**

| ESRI type | GeoJSON type |
|-----------|-------------|
| `esriGeometryPoint` | `Point` |
| `esriGeometryMultipoint` | `MultiPoint` |
| `esriGeometryPolyline` | `MultiLineString` |
| `esriGeometryPolygon` | `MultiPolygon` |
| `esriGeometryEnvelope` | `Polygon` |
| Unknown / missing | `GeometryCollection` (fallback) |

---

### 2. Load strategies

The `arcgis-feature` layer will support three loading strategies, configurable via `options.strategy` (default: `tile`). The strategy will be persisted in the map configuration.

#### Query parameters

All strategies will send requests to `{featureServerUrl}/{layerId}/query` with:

| Parameter | Value | Purpose |
|-----------|-------|---------|
| `f` | `geojson` | Response format — native GeoJSON, no conversion needed |
| `where` | `1=1` | Match all features |
| `outFields` | `*` | Return all attributes |
| `outSR` | `4326` | Response coordinates in EPSG:4326 |
| `inSR` | `4326` | Input geometry CRS (bbox/tile strategies) |
| `geometry` | `xmin,ymin,xmax,ymax` | Envelope filter (bbox/tile strategies) |
| `geometryType` | `esriGeometryEnvelope` | Geometry filter type (bbox/tile strategies) |
| `spatialRel` | `esriSpatialRelIntersects` | Spatial relationship (bbox/tile strategies) |
| `resultOffset` | `0, N, 2N, ...` | Pagination offset |
| `resultRecordCount` | `maxRecordCount` or `1000` | Page size — will use service's `maxRecordCount` when available |

#### Strategies

| Strategy | Default | OL mechanism | Cesium mechanism | Notes |
|----------|---------|-------------|-----------------|-------|
| `tile` | Yes | `ol/loadingstrategy/tile` with XYZ grid | `TiledBillboardCollection` | Fetches features per tile cell. In Cesium, **point/multipoint only** — non-point layers will auto-downgrade to `bbox` |
| `bbox` | — | `ol/loadingstrategy/bbox` | `camera.moveEnd` listener (debounced 300ms) | Fetches features for the current viewport extent |
| `all` | — | `ol/loadingstrategy/all` | Single fetch on layer add | Fetches all features via paginated requests |

#### Pagination

FeatureServer enforces `maxRecordCount` per request. A `fetchAllPages` helper will paginate using `resultOffset` / `resultRecordCount` until the response's `exceededTransferLimit` flag is `false`. Page size will default to the service's advertised `maxRecordCount` (fallback: 1000). Duplicate features will be filtered via OBJECTID tracking.

